*Step 4 (the support on $U$).* By definition $x\in\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal F)$ if and only if $\mathcal F_x
eq0$ [def-weil-pbc-closed-subset-proper-over-base](2), i.e. (Step 3) if and only if $M_{\mathfrak p_x}
eq0$, i.e. $\mathfrak p_x\in\operatorname{Supp}(M)$. Since $M$ is finitely generated (Step 1), [lem-weil-pbc-finite-module-support-annihilator] gives $M_{\mathfrak p_x}
eq0\iff\operatorname{Ann}_A(M)\subseteq\mathfrak p_x$. Hence, identifying $U$ with $\operatorname{Spec}A$ via $g$, $\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal F)\cap U=g(V(\operatorname{Ann}_A(M)))$.
